node_modules/
dist/

# This repo installs with npm - package-lock.json is the lockfile. Bun is here
# only as the test runner (`bun test`), which does not install. A stray
# `bun install` would drop a committable lockfile and give the repo a second,
# independently-resolved dependency tree. The glob covers both formats: bun.lock
# (text, default since 1.2) and bun.lockb (binary, older versions) - whoever
# reaches for a bun command here might be on any version, so a pattern that only
# caught the one CI pins today would not be much of a guard.
bun.lock*

.env
.env.local
*.log
.DS_Store
CLAUDE.md
**/CLAUDE.md
.omc/
.claude/
.entire/
.impeccable/
